ArcMap Modernization – Key Achievements and Business Impact

1. Modernization of a Company-Wide Geospatial Library

Played a key role in modernizing ArcMap, a critical geospatial mapping library used across the company. The modernization involved transforming an aging technology foundation into a modern, scalable, and reusable solution built on ArcGIS Maps SDK 5.x, including version 5.0.19, and LitElement. This was not just a technology upgrade but a major transformation to strengthen the company’s geospatial capabilities and support future business requirements.

2. Importance of Geospatial Technology in Railroad Operations

Geospatial technology plays an important role in the railroad industry, where tracks, infrastructure, assets, and operations are spread across thousands of miles. It helps applications visualize geographic information, understand asset locations, investigate operational data, and support informed decision-making. ArcMap provides the common mapping foundation that enables different applications across the company to deliver these capabilities.

3. Development of Reusable Mapping Capabilities

Developed and enhanced reusable mapping components that support interactive maps, geographic data visualization, drawing and editing, measurement tools, map layers, information popups, and location-based interactions. These capabilities allow different application teams to integrate mapping functionality without building everything from scratch, improving consistency and reducing duplicate development efforts.

4. Enterprise-Wide Business Value

ArcMap is not limited to a single application. It serves as a shared geospatial foundation across the company, including applications such as Geo app and AT app. Modernizing this library creates long-term business value by improving maintainability, simplifying future enhancements, supporting consistent user experiences, and helping application teams respond more efficiently to evolving business needs.

5. Significant Ownership and Delivery of Geo App

Demonstrated strong ownership by contributing approximately 95% of the development of one of the three user interfaces within Geo app. Successfully integrated the modernized ArcMap library with application-specific functionality, delivering an interactive and user-friendly experience. This work demonstrated the practical value of the modernized library in supporting business applications.

6. Enhancing AT App and Geographic Data Visualization

Contributed to AT app improvements, including UI redesign, map integration, interactive features, and time-based geographic visualization. These enhancements help users explore geographic information more effectively, understand changes across different periods, and interact with complex data through a more intuitive interface.

7. Technical Leadership and Cross-Team Collaboration

Went beyond assigned development responsibilities by supporting other application teams with ArcMap integration, troubleshooting, knowledge sharing, demonstrations, and code reviews. Proactively addressed complex challenges and focused on reusable solutions that could benefit multiple applications rather than implementing isolated fixes.

8. Long-Term Value and Future Readiness

The modernization helped reduce dependency on aging technology and established a stronger foundation for future innovation. By providing a common mapping solution, ArcMap helps minimize repeated development efforts, supports easier integration, and enables the company to introduce new geospatial capabilities more efficiently.

Overall Achievement Summary

The key achievement was not simply developing new features or upgrading technology, but modernizing a critical geospatial foundation used across the company and demonstrating its value through real business applications.

Through ArcMap modernization, significant ownership of Geo app development, contributions to AT app, and continuous support for other development teams, the work has helped strengthen the company’s geospatial capabilities, improve application usability, promote technology reuse, and create sustainable long-term business value.

These contributions demonstrate strong ownership, technical leadership, proactive problem-solving, cross-team collaboration, and a consistent commitment to delivering value beyond assigned responsibilities.